AB  - The study aims to investigate the combined effects of the replacement of cement by alccofine and coarse aggregate by granite waste on the mechanical properties of M25 grade concrete. Alccofine-1203 is an ultrafine supplementary cementitious material produced through a controlled granulation technique, resulting in a highly reactive, glass-rich composition. Because concrete is widely used in construction, such reactive additives are increasingly important for improving its performance.The improvement of cementitious material becomes more and more essential. The main aim of the investigation is to study the effect of Alccofine mix by varying content such as 0%,8%, 9%, 10%, 11%, 12%,13% and 14% and finding its optimum content. The investigation focused on evaluating compressive and flexural strength after 7, 28, 56, and 90 days of water curing. The results indicated a consistent improvement in both strength parameters across all replacement levels examined. The samples with added Alccofine of 10% replacement in cement showed better results in comparison with the others. When Alccofine is used as a partial replacement for cement beyond the 10% level, both compressive and flexural strengths tend to decline. In this study, concrete mixes were prepared by substituting coarse aggregate with granite waste in varying proportions of 10%, 20%, 30%, 40%, and 50% to identify the most effective percentage of Alccofine. The performance of these mixes was evaluated at curing periods of 7, 28, 56, and 90 days.The samples with Alccofine of 10% and 30% granite waste showed better results in comparison with the others.
