AB  - CRISTALL Project presents an innovative zero-waste technology for processing mining tailings into high-quality artificial stone materials (granite, basalt, diabase, jasper and others). The method is based on controlled melting and crystallization of silicate-rich industrial waste, resulting in durable construction materials that meet geological and engineering standards. The project demonstrates: • transformation of tailings into valuable stone analogues; • elimination of waste storage and environmental impact; • production of materials suitable for construction, architecture, hydraulic engineering, and industrial applications; • potential recovery of metal components during processing. This document provides a concise overview of the CRISTALL technology, its principles, benefits, and potential industrial scalability. Author: Oleg Khatsaev, Founder and Project Leader, CRISTALL Initiative.
