AB  - Natural stone products hold potential to be a low-carbon material for construction of walls, embankments, and pavements. Their tactility and appearance evoke biophilia and, with locally sourced stone, a deep connection to a place. But the current supply chain of the dimension stone industry is global with stone quarried in one country, worked in another, then used in a third country accumulating a tremendous carbon footprint through its transport. Forced and child labor in some countries makes internationally sourced stone less economically expensive, but it comes at a high human cost. The chapter focuses on environmental impacts and human health and equity across the life cycle of stone and discusses the ANSI/NSC 373 Sustainable Production of Natural Dimension Stone Standard. Types, qualities, and performance of stone are discussed along with maintenance of stone structures.
